The post hoc injury risk meta-analysis was performed on the three studies that used supervision [46–48]. Two studies showed negative log risk ratios that did not differ from zero [46, 48], and the pooled log risk ratio of − 0.77 (95% CI − 1.18 to − 0.37) was statistically significant in favor of the intervention (z = − 3.75, p < 0.001; Fig. 6). No significant heterogeneity between true outcomes were found by Q test (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
